 watching him  in a microcosm of a sort of a one murder  situation um he's now doing it on a  million murder type of situation basis  with ukraine  and what i'm so fearful of is that um he  isn't gonna back down in ukraine that if  he  is seen to be weak he will just do  something even more terrible and i i  dread to think what that's going to be  he also cares a lot about money his  money that's what got you into trouble  with them in the first place there was a  tax fraud that your company was pursuing  and you determined that putin himself  was profiting it makes me think that  sanctions if they hurt him personally  might have an effect do you agree or not  i totally agree so putin values  money more than human life and he's got  a lot of money i think he's worth 200  north of 200 billion dollars  and um he doesn't keep that money in his  own name he keeps that money in the name  of these oligarchs we all know about the  oligarchs with their yachts and so on  um and so if we want to sanction  vladimir putin we've got to sanction the  oligarchs and we're starting to do that  right now  and um even if he's not seeing it he is  seething right now thinking that his  money is no longer available to him but  let's talk about you bill for a second  because so many people who are working  with you  starting with your with your lawyer so  many people who are helping you in this  case are no longer with us i mean you  get a phone call that says i don't mean  to alarm you but never a good way when  the phone call comes and what were you  told in that phone call why does putin  still want to get you but so this was a  phone call from from a senior government  official u.s government official to say  that there is a kidnapping plot being  organized by the russians  to try to kidnap me take me back to  russia too effectively to probably kill  me  um  why do they want that because um i was  going after their money uh why was i  going after their money because my  lawyer sergey 